<package xmlns="http://www.idpf.org/2007/opf" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/" xmlns:dcterms="http://purl.org/dc/terms/" version="3.0" unique-identifier="pub-identifier" prefix="ibooks: http://vocabulary.itunes.apple.com/rdf/ibooks/vocabulary-extensions-1.0/"><metadata><dc:identifier id="pub-identifier">978-1-098-10013-1</dc:identifier><meta id="meta-identifier" property="dcterms:identifier">978-1-098-10013-1</meta><dc:title id="pub-title">Learning Domain-Driven Design (for Ana Barrios)</dc:title><meta property="dcterms:title" id="meta-title">Learning Domain-Driven Design</meta><dc:language id="pub-language">en</dc:language><meta property="dcterms:language" id="meta-language">en</meta><meta property="dcterms:modified">2024-03-18T14:12:54Z</meta><dc:publisher>O'Reilly Media, Inc.</dc:publisher><meta property="dcterms:publisher">O'Reilly Media, Inc.</meta><dc:date>2021-10-15</dc:date><meta property="dcterms:date">2021-10-15</meta><dc:description>Building software is harder than ever. As a developer, you not only have to chase ever-changing technological trends but also need to understand the business domains behind the software. This practical book provides you with a set of core patterns, principles, and practices for analyzing business domains, understanding business strategy, and, most importantly, aligning software design with its business needs.</dc:description><meta property="dcterms:description">Building software is harder than ever. As a developer, you not only have to chase ever-changing technological trends but also need to understand the business domains behind the software. This practical book provides you with a set of core patterns, principles, and practices for analyzing business domains, understanding business strategy, and, most importantly, aligning software design with its business needs.</meta><dc:creator>Vlad Khononov</dc:creator><meta property="dcterms:creator">Vlad Khononov</meta><meta name="cover" content="cover-image"/><meta propert